        "original_id": "ffcf4de1-5d20-5397-937b-af713da082f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Shane Meadows\n- Works: This Is England, sequel series\n- Topics: independent film, skinheads, far-right adoption of subculture, West Indies cultural roots, ska, soul, reggae\n- Places: England\n\nFacts:\n- Shane Meadows was born on 26 December 1972 and is an English filmmaker of independent film.\n- In 2006, Shane Meadows wrote and directed the British drama film This Is England.\n- This Is England is one of Shane Meadows's best-known works, along with its three sequel series released from 2010 to 2015.\n- This Is England centres on young skinheads in England in 1983.\n- This Is England depicts the skinhead subculture as rooted in 1960s West Indies culture, especially ska, soul, and reggae music.\n- This Is England shows how the skinhead subculture was adopted by the far-right, especially white nationalists and white supremacists, causing divisions within the skinhead scene.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
